---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout title="about" current="about">
  <article class="prose">
    <figure class="crest">
      <img src="/emblem.png" width="360" height="360" alt={`The ${site.name} maker's seal: a bearded pirate skull in a ship's wheel, over crossed cutlasses, above an "x-hakt" banner.`} />
    </figure>

    <h1 style="font-size:1.6rem;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin-bottom:1rem">about</h1>

    <p>
      A captain with no ship and no crew keeps a log anyway. That is this site. I
      spend my days fixing technical problems and drawing up solutions, mostly on
      one small mesh of servers, and I write down how each piece is actually
      wired so the next person does not have to reverse-engineer it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every entry is a practitioner describing their own setup, with one diagram
      carrying the idea. If you came here looking for <em>how</em> rather than
      <em>whether</em>, you are in the right place. Entries are signed <code>-x</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>The pirate streak</h2>
    <p>
      It is a maker's mark and a turn of phrase, nothing more. The seal above is
      real artwork; a few corners of the interface borrow a word from the sea
      (the map, the spyglass). The filing itself is plain: notes are grouped by
      the kind of work they are, and tagged with the technology they use. If a
      nautical label ever gets in the way of finding something, that is a bug.
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Sibling of <a href="https://control.x-hakt.com">Control Room</a>, the
      private dashboard that runs the same infrastructure: same dark palette,
      same two typefaces, same restraint. Built with Astro and MDX, prerendered
      to static files, served behind Traefik on the same box it documents.
      Diagrams are drawn as SVG and read by a human before they ship. Type is
      IBM Plex Mono and IBM Plex Sans.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .crest {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .crest img {
    width: 260px;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 60%;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .crest img { width: 180px; }
  }
</style>
